IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sssa-nouns`
IMPORT `sssa-part2-scheme`

-- Tests for sssa-part2-scheme.l4 (ss 5 to 7).  Every expected value is written
-- from the text of the provision, beside the assertion, before the run.
-- A `Birth facts` is built positionally: the ruler above each block names the
-- fields in their declared order (year, month, day), each a MAYBE NUMBER where
-- NOTHING means "cannot be ascertained".
-- Numbers standing for amounts and classes that the regulations would prescribe
-- are stand-ins invented for the test; the Act gives none.

§ `Tests -- Part 2`

§§ `s 5(1)`

#ASSERT `s 5(1) the name by which the established scheme is known` EQUALS "Silver Support Scheme"
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the purpose for which the Scheme is established` EQUALS "providing financial support to eligible individuals"

§§ `s 6(2)(c) and (d) deemed day and month`

-- (d): month cannot be ascertained -> January; otherwise the month stands.
-- fields:                      year,       month,      day
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(d) the month of birth taken for s 6(1)(b)` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), NOTHING, (JUST 15)) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(d) the month of birth taken for s 6(1)(b)` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 5), (JUST 15)) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(d) the month of birth taken for s 6(1)(b)` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 12), NOTHING) EQUALS 12

-- (c): day cannot be ascertained -> the first day of that month; otherwise the day stands.
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(c) the day of the month of birth taken for s 6(1)(b)` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 3), NOTHING) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(c) the day of the month of birth taken for s 6(1)(b)` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 3), (JUST 15)) EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(c) the day of the month of birth taken for s 6(1)(b)` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 3), (JUST 31)) EQUALS 31

§§ `s 6(2)(a) and (b) the 65th anniversary`

-- (a): the 65th anniversary of the date of birth is the same day and month 65 years on.
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) and (b) the 65th anniversary of the date of birth` 1960 3 15 EQUALS Date 15 3 2025
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) and (b) the 65th anniversary of the date of birth` 1960 1 1 EQUALS Date 1 1 2025
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) and (b) the 65th anniversary of the date of birth` 1960 12 31 EQUALS Date 31 12 2025
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) and (b) the 65th anniversary of the date of birth` 1959 2 28 EQUALS Date 28 2 2024
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) and (b) the 65th anniversary of the date of birth` 1960 3 1 EQUALS Date 1 3 2025

-- (b): born on 29 February -> 1 March, whether the birth year is an ordinary leap year (1960, 1996) or a century leap year (2000).
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) and (b) the 65th anniversary of the date of birth` 1960 2 29 EQUALS Date 1 3 2025
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) and (b) the 65th anniversary of the date of birth` 1996 2 29 EQUALS Date 1 3 2061
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) and (b) the 65th anniversary of the date of birth` 2000 2 29 EQUALS Date 1 3 2065

§§ `s 6(2) the date on which an individual attains 65`

-- fields:                                                                                 year,       month,      day
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 3), (JUST 15)) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 3 2025)
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 2), (JUST 29)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2025)
-- (c): day cannot be ascertained -> first of the month.
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 3), NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2025)
-- (d): month cannot be ascertained -> January (FORK F-2: the ascertained day is kept, so the 15th of January).
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), NOTHING, (JUST 15)) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2025)
-- (c) and (d) together: the first day of January.
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), NOTHING, NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2025)
-- (d) with a day of 29: the month is January, so there is no 29 February in the case.
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), NOTHING, (JUST 29)) EQUALS JUST (Date 29 1 2025)
-- The year cannot be ascertained: the text deems a month and a day and is silent on the year.
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF NOTHING, (JUST 3), (JUST 15)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 6(1)(b) has attained 65 years of age: the day before, the day of and the day after`

-- Born 15 March 1960: the 65th anniversary is 15 March 2025.
-- fields:                                                                  year,       month,      day              date asked about
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 3), (JUST 15)) (Date 14 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 3), (JUST 15)) (Date 15 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 3), (JUST 15)) (Date 16 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Born 29 February 1960: the 65th anniversary is deemed to occur on 1 March 2025 (not 28 February, where a years-added clamp would put it).
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 2), (JUST 29)) (Date 28 2 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 2), (JUST 29)) (Date 1 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 2), (JUST 29)) (Date 2 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Born 29 February 1996: deemed 1 March 2061.
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1996), (JUST 2), (JUST 29)) (Date 28 2 2061) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1996), (JUST 2), (JUST 29)) (Date 1 3 2061) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1996), (JUST 2), (JUST 29)) (Date 2 3 2061) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Born 1 March 1960: the same 1 March 2025 as a leap-day birth.
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 3), (JUST 1)) (Date 28 2 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 3), (JUST 1)) (Date 1 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 3), (JUST 1)) (Date 2 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Born in March 1960, day cannot be ascertained: deemed the 1st (s 6(2)(c)).
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 3), NOTHING) (Date 28 2 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 3), NOTHING) (Date 1 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 3), NOTHING) (Date 2 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Born in 1960, month cannot be ascertained but the 15th is known: deemed 15 January (FORK F-2).
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), NOTHING, (JUST 15)) (Date 14 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), NOTHING, (JUST 15)) (Date 15 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), NOTHING, (JUST 15)) (Date 16 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Born in 1960, neither month nor day known: deemed 1 January.
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), NOTHING, NOTHING) (Date 31 12 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), NOTHING, NOTHING) (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), NOTHING, NOTHING) (Date 2 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Born 31 December 1960: the anniversary is 31 December 2025; the day after is in the next year.
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 12), (JUST 31)) (Date 30 12 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 12), (JUST 31)) (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 12), (JUST 31)) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Far from the anniversary on either side.
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1900), (JUST 3), (JUST 15)) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 2000), (JUST 3), (JUST 15)) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The year cannot be ascertained: no date can be worked out, so the answer is NOTHING at any date asked about.
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF NOTHING, (JUST 3), (JUST 15)) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`Birth facts` OF NOTHING, (JUST 3), (JUST 15)) (Date 1 1 1990) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 6(1) eligible individual`

-- inputs: citizen, birth facts, date asked about, other criteria met (MAYBE BOOLEAN).
-- Born 15 March 1960: 65 on 15 March 2025.
-- all three limbs met
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` TRUE (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 3), (JUST 15)) (Date 15 3 2025) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not a citizen: (a) fails
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` FALSE (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 3), (JUST 15)) (Date 15 3 2025) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a citizen the day before 65: (b) fails
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` TRUE (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 3), (JUST 15)) (Date 14 3 2025) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the prescribed criteria are not met: (c) fails
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` TRUE (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 3), (JUST 15)) (Date 15 3 2025) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- whether the prescribed criteria are met is not known
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` TRUE (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 3), (JUST 15)) (Date 15 3 2025) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- the year of birth cannot be ascertained: the age limb is not known
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` TRUE (`Birth facts` OF NOTHING, (JUST 3), (JUST 15)) (Date 15 3 2025) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` TRUE (`Birth facts` OF NOTHING, (JUST 3), (JUST 15)) (Date 15 3 2025) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- one limb failing answers no even where another limb is not known
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` FALSE (`Birth facts` OF NOTHING, (JUST 3), (JUST 15)) (Date 15 3 2025) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` TRUE (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 3), (JUST 15)) (Date 14 3 2025) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` TRUE (`Birth facts` OF NOTHING, (JUST 3), (JUST 15)) (Date 15 3 2025) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a leap-day birth: not 65 on 28 February 2025, 65 on 1 March 2025
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` TRUE (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 2), (JUST 29)) (Date 28 2 2025) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` TRUE (`Birth facts` OF (JUST 1960), (JUST 2), (JUST 29)) (Date 1 3 2025) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 7(1) benefits`

-- the grant is to an eligible individual
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the individual is eligible to receive the benefits that may be prescribed` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a person who is not an eligible individual is outside the grant; the section does not say that person receives nothing
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the individual is eligible to receive the benefits that may be prescribed` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the individual is eligible to receive the benefits that may be prescribed` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- amount: 777 stands in for an amount the regulations prescribe
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the amount of benefit an eligible individual is eligible to receive` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 777) EQUALS JUST 777
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the amount of benefit an eligible individual is eligible to receive` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the amount of benefit an eligible individual is eligible to receive` (JUST FALSE) (JUST 777) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the amount of benefit an eligible individual is eligible to receive` NOTHING (JUST 777) EQUALS NOTHING

-- manner: "by the manner prescribed" stands in for the manner the regulations prescribe
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the manner in which an eligible individual is to receive the benefit` (JUST TRUE) (JUST "the manner prescribed") EQUALS JUST "the manner prescribed"
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the manner in which an eligible individual is to receive the benefit` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the manner in which an eligible individual is to receive the benefit` (JUST FALSE) (JUST "the manner prescribed") EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the manner in which an eligible individual is to receive the benefit` NOTHING (JUST "the manner prescribed") EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 7(2) different classes`

-- two classes with stand-in amounts, 11 and 22
GIVETH A LIST OF `Class amount`
`two stand-in classes` MEANS
    LIST
        (`Class amount` OF "class one", 11)
      , (`Class amount` OF "class two", 22)

#ASSERT `s 7(2) the amount prescribed for the class of eligible individual` "class one" `two stand-in classes` EQUALS JUST 11
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the amount prescribed for the class of eligible individual` "class two" `two stand-in classes` EQUALS JUST 22
-- a class the table does not list: the regulations are outside the sources
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the amount prescribed for the class of eligible individual` "class three" `two stand-in classes` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the amount prescribed for the class of eligible individual` "class one" EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
